// Nettle

@100 = ~Nettle~
@101 = ~Nettle~
@102 = ~NETTLE: A halfling that slips past wards and stabs the magic out of a caster. The Nettle's backstab never grows past double damage. Instead it breaches, drains and spoils the caster it lands on, and its traps carry the same sting.

Advantages:
– Spoiling Backstab: a backstab does double damage at every level, and leaves the target with a 30% chance to fail spells and -2 to saves against spells for 3 rounds. From level 7 it also drains the target's highest-level memorised wizard spell; from level 11 it Breaches the target, with no save, ignoring magic resistance; from level 15 the chance to fail spells rises to 50% and the target loses 20% magic resistance; from level 19 it strips one spell protection; from level 23 it strips one spell protection each round for 3 rounds.
– Spoiling Traps: the Nettle's traps do no damage. The creature that sets one off suffers the full Spoiling Backstab; anyone else caught suffers the chance to fail spells and the saves penalty.
– Stubborn Will: +2 to saves against spells and wands; immune to charm, to confusion from level 6, and to domination from level 10.
– Sure Hand: +1 to hit, plus 1 more every 5 levels, up to +5 at level 21.
– Quiet Feet: +15% to Hide in Shadows and Move Silently.
– Not Fooled: +20% to Detect Illusion.
– Unnoticed: permanent Non-Detection from level 9.
– Small and Nimble: +2 AC.

Disadvantages:
– Backstabs stay at double damage: the multiplier never rises with level.
– May only use daggers, short swords, clubs, darts, slings and short bows.
– Cannot use wands or scrolls.
– Lore is 0 and cannot be raised.
– Requires Dexterity 15 or higher.
– Must be a neutral good or chaotic good halfling.~

@110 = ~Nettle~
@111 = ~The Nettle's stubborn will, sure hand and quiet feet.~

@120 = ~Spoiling Backstab~
@121 = ~Spoiling Backstab

The target suffers a chance to fail spells and a penalty to saves against spells for 3 rounds, with more effects as the Nettle rises in level.~
@122 = ~Spoiled!~

@130 = ~Spoiling Snare~
@131 = ~Spoiling Snare

Sets a trap that does no damage. The creature that sets it off suffers the full Spoiling Backstab for the Nettle's level; anyone else caught suffers the chance to fail spells and the saves penalty.~

@140 = ~Underfoot~
@141 = ~Underfoot

The Nettle instantly hides in shadows, even while seen. In a busy fight, nobody keeps track of a halfling.~

@145 = ~Disenchanting Strike~
@146 = ~Disenchanting Strike

For 1 round, every hit strips one spell protection from its target, as Secret Word.~

@150 = ~Common Sense~
@151 = ~Common Sense

For 1 turn, the Nettle and its allies nearby are immune to charm, confusion and domination.~

@155 = ~Make-Believe~
@156 = ~Make-Believe

Summoned creatures around the Nettle are destroyed. Only summoned creatures are affected.~

@160 = ~Unravelling Trap~
@161 = ~Unravelling Trap

Sets a special Spoiling Trap. On top of the usual Spoiling Trap effects, everyone caught is hit by Remove Magic at the Nettle's level, stripping their buffs.~

@180 = ~Nettles cannot use this item.~
